Z||000000||Haze_Performance||11-19-2001||01:58 AM||||Well, I was surfing around & came across <A HREF="http://www.indiglogauges.com" TARGET=_blank>www.indiglogauges.com</A>  . There website says "<FONT COLOR="red">PLEASE NOTE: IF YOU DO NOT SEE YOUR VEHICLE MODEL LISTED THEN WE DO NOT SELL IT!</FONT>" But I emailed them anyway. (Why not? It wont hurt right?) Anyway... If there was enough interest, I would think they might go for the idea... (Just a thought)  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> If your interested... give-em a email.. <BR><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/goodlife.gif">    <BR><FONT SIZE="1"><FONT COLOR="purple">Goto Website - <A HREF="http://www.ClassicFiero.com" TARGET=_blank>Click Here</A> </FONT></FONT>||||reg||14
Z||000001||Mach10||11-19-2001||02:20 AM||||well the indiglo part of it is just a treated layer. get one that has faces about the right size and hack it to pieces... ||||reg||4
Z||000002||Nashco||11-19-2001||02:51 AM||||I had an email from somebody on ebay that was selling indiglo faces for the older 80 mph speedo setup (not backlit).  They said they made it for the backlit style, 120 mph units, but a 200 dollar pricetag for only the tach and speedo, all the others being additional...I said no thanks.  I know they're out there somewhere, but for a ridiculous price.<P>Oh, before you ask me, I don't know who it was, I deleted the email long ago.<P>*edit* There are some forum members working on indiglo style guages.  I remember MinnGreenGT is one of them, anybody have an update on the status of that project?<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT<p>[This message has been edited by Nashco (edited 11-19-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Haze_Performance||11-19-2001||03:53 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Nashco:<BR><B>I had an email from somebody on ebay that was selling indiglo faces for the older 80 mph speedo setup (not backlit).  They said they made it for the backlit style, 120 mph units, but a 200 dollar pricetag for only the tach and speedo, all the others being additional...I said no thanks.  I know they're out there somewhere, but for a ridiculous price.<P>Oh, before you ask me, I don't know who it was, I deleted the email long ago.<P>*edit* There are some forum members working on indiglo style guages.  I remember MinnGreenGT is one of them, anybody have an update on the status of that project?<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT<P>[This message has been edited by Nashco (edited 11-19-2001).]</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>I know of the guy your talking about... I emailed him some time ago. (When I saw it on ebay) His had graphics on the gauges that I didn't like. (Ricer stuff) As for Minn.. I've been following his idea to. (Very cool) He was having some lighting problems (not sure if he fixed it yet?)... I was just wondering if there was a company out there that would think of making ones for the Fiero...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/goodlife.gif">    <BR><FONT SIZE="1"><FONT COLOR="purple">Goto Website - <A HREF="http://www.ClassicFiero.com" TARGET=_blank>Click Here</A> </FONT></FONT>||||reg||14
Z||000004||MinnGreenGT||11-19-2001||09:56 AM||||Hey guys!  Good memories... I've been messing around with the backlit designs for awhile now, but as stated above, I had trouble with the stock light source ( <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/011111.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/011111.html</A>  ).  I've contacted a few ElectroLuminescent Paper suppliers, but the only reasonable thing I've come across is a base kit for about $100- and I currently don't have the funds to go that way.  So I'm in the process of finishing a set of white face gauges with lit numbers instead of the face... it'll be a temporary fix until I can find a reasonable supplier for the EL paper.  If you want to contact the company and let them know that we have vector-art for all the necessary gauges, I'd gladly send it to them to try to have them make 'em!  LMK!<P>------------------<BR>              <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/GreenGT6.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Nashco||11-19-2001||10:49 AM||||Sweet deal Rob, I'm excited to see what you come up with.  It seems no matter how fast I try to get stuff done, you're always one step ahead with your projects!  Well, I've got a few under wraps, so hopefully you aren't thinking these ones up already! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
